  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "All 489 tests pass (`python -m compileall app`, `pytest -q`).\n\n**What I changed**\n\nUC2 — contract document generation (`POST /api/v1/contracts`):\n- New `app/services/contract_documents.py`: merges `{{mergeField}}` placeholders in the template body from the contract/counterparty/owner, and writes the contract's Version 1 — a `contract_documents` row plus a `contract_versions` row numbered 1. With third-party paper the uploaded file becomes Version 1 verbatim (name/type/size preserved, no merge).\n- `app/services/contracts.py` calls it inside the create transaction; `ContractResponse` gains two additive optional fields `documentVersionNumber` and `message` (\"Contract created successfully and saved as Draft\"). The shared contract's `ContractResponse` (id/contractName/status) is unchanged in spelling.\n- Added `insert_document` / `insert_contract_version` to `app/repositories/contract_lifecycle.py`.\n\nUC5 — risk re-check after external changes:\n- `app/services/lifecycle_clauses.py`: `apply_external_redlines` (applies the counterparty's clause changes and returns exactly the changed clause ids; falls back to \"clause text no longer present in the returned document\" for a plain redline), `reanalyze_clauses` (re-scores only those clauses; overall score follows), and a failure path that records a retryable state.\n- `POST .../external/{linkToken}/submit` commits the new version **before** the re-check, so an AI failure never loses the version; the contract then reports `analysisStatus: \"Failed\"` from `GET .../clause-analysis`, and `POST .../retry-extraction` re-scores exactly the pending clauses. `ExternalSubmitRequest` gains an optional `clauseRedlines` list (documented in-file) so the diff and the re-check know which clauses changed.\n- Contract-naming fix: `VersionSummaryResponse.source` is now `\"Internal\"`/`\"External\"` (was lowercase), with old rows normalised on read. `GET .../negotiation` already 404s before routing, `compare` already takes `versionA`/`versionB`, and `ClauseDiffResponse.clauseId` already equals `ClauseResponse.clauseId` — left as-is.\n- New tests: `tests/test_contract_documents.py`, `tests/test_lifecycle_uc5_recheck.py`.\n\nReading taken: the two numbered items are backend capabilities, so both were built end to end; the endpoint list in the counterpart note describes routes this repo already serves, so I only touched the naming/behaviour the two items require. No migration was needed (all tables already exist), which matters because `alembic/versions/` is outside the paths I may modify. I also could not run the uvicorn curl pass — this environment has no reachable Postgres, so verification was via the SQLite-backed test suite.",
  "files_changed": [
    "app/repositories/contract_lifecycle.py",
    "app/repositories/lifecycle_clauses.py",
    "app/schemas/contract.py",
    "app/schemas/lifecycle_negotiation.py",
