    "notes": "UC5 re-check confirmed: VersionSummaryResponse.source is now normalized to exactly 'Internal'/'External'; ClauseDiffResponse.clauseId is populated from the version snapshots and is the same uuid string as ClauseResponse.clauseId; GET .../negotiation returns 404 (not an empty 200) when no routing row exists. GET .../compare requires versionA and versionB as query params (no defaults — omitting them is a 422). analysisStatus values the code emits are 'Completed', 'Failed' and 'Blocked'; a failed post-redline re-analysis also forces proceedToNegotiationEnabled=false, and POST .../retry-extraction re-scores exactly the clauses the counterparty changed. The external submit accepts an optional clauseRedlines array ([{clauseId, clauseText}]) — without it the backend infers changed clauses by matching current clause text against redlineText, which is lossy, so the frontend should send clauseRedlines when it can. GET /api/v1/templates accepts only status and contractType (no industry filter). ContractResponse is much wider than the three fields the frontend declares and now additionally carries documentVersionNumber and message; the frontend's narrower type still parses. Roles: GET .../negotiation allows CONTRACT_OWNER/LEGAL_REVIEWER/APPROVER/TENANT_ADMIN, POST .../routing is CONTRACT_OWNER only, GET .../compare excludes TENANT_ADMIN, POST .../retry-extraction is LEGAL_REVIEWER/CONTRACT_OWNER only. No endpoint from the counterpart's contract is missing here."
